{"key":"nlp-basics-u1-02","seriesId":"nlp-basics","episode":"u1-02","title":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","fps":30,"duration":254.357,"durationInFrames":7631,"video":{"width":1920,"height":1080,"burnCaptions":true,"brand":"learnvi.in"},"badge":["UNIT 1 · LESSON 2","TOKENIZATION"],"series":{"title":"NLP, Simply Explained","subtitle":"University NLP, one idea at a time, no heavy maths","runningPrompt":"","stops":[{"id":"u1-01","number":1,"name":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","stamp":"THE STAGES OF NLP: FROM LETTERS TO MEANING","topic":""},{"id":"u1-02","number":2,"name":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","stamp":"TOKENIZATION: HOW TEXT BECOMES PIECES","topic":""},{"id":"u1-03","number":3,"name":"Text Classification: Teaching Computers to Sort Text","stamp":"TEXT CLASSIFICATION: TEACHING COMPUTERS TO SORT TEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u1-04","number":4,"name":"Language Models: Guessing the Next Word","stamp":"LANGUAGE MODELS: GUESSING THE NEXT WORD","topic":""},{"id":"u2-01","number":5,"name":"Morphology: The Building Blocks Inside Words","stamp":"MORPHOLOGY: THE BUILDING BLOCKS INSIDE WORDS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-02","number":6,"name":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","stamp":"PART-OF-SPEECH TAGGING: IS IT A NOUN OR A VERB?","topic":""},{"id":"u2-03","number":7,"name":"Chunking: Grouping Words into Phrases","stamp":"CHUNKING: GROUPING WORDS INTO PHRASES","topic":""},{"id":"u2-04","number":8,"name":"Generative vs Discriminative Models","stamp":"GENERATIVE VS DISCRIMINATIVE MODELS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-05","number":9,"name":"Hidden Markov Models, Intuitively","stamp":"HIDDEN MARKOV MODELS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u2-06","number":10,"name":"Conditional Random Fields, Intuitively","stamp":"CONDITIONAL RANDOM FIELDS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u3-01","number":11,"name":"Constituency Parsing: Sentences as Trees","stamp":"CONSTITUENCY PARSING: SENTENCES AS TREES","topic":""},{"id":"u3-02","number":12,"name":"Dependency Parsing: Who Did What to Whom","stamp":"DEPENDENCY PARSING: WHO DID WHAT TO WHOM","topic":""},{"id":"u3-03","number":13,"name":"Transition-Based Parsing: Building Trees Step by Step","stamp":"TRANSITION-BASED PARSING: BUILDING TREES STEP BY STEP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-01","number":14,"name":"Word Vectors: Giving Words a Place on a Map","stamp":"WORD VECTORS: GIVING WORDS A PLACE ON A MAP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-02","number":15,"name":"Word2Vec: Learning Word Vectors from Context","stamp":"WORD2VEC: LEARNING WORD VECTORS FROM CONTEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u4-03","number":16,"name":"Recurrent Neural Networks: Reading with Memory","stamp":"RECURRENT NEURAL NETWORKS: READING WITH MEMORY","topic":""},{"id":"u4-04","number":17,"name":"LSTMs: Remembering What Matters","stamp":"LSTMS: REMEMBERING WHAT MATTERS","topic":""},{"id":"u5-01","number":18,"name":"Contextual Embeddings and ELMo","stamp":"CONTEXTUAL EMBEDDINGS AND ELMO","topic":""},{"id":"u5-02","number":19,"name":"BERT: Reading in Both Directions","stamp":"BERT: READING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS","topic":""}]},"stop":{"number":2,"name":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","stamp":"TOKENIZATION: HOW TEXT BECOMES PIECES"},"shorts":{"width":1080,"height":1920,"maxSeconds":60,"cta":"Full lesson: NLP, Simply Explained · Unit 1"},"thumbnail":{"headline":"How AI cuts text into pieces","big":"rain + drops"},"segments":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","component":"TitleCard","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c01","start":0.6,"end":6.515,"marks":{},"text":"Welcome back to NLP, Simply Explained. This is unit 1, lesson 2: tokenization.","words":[{"w":"Welcome","start":0.6},{"w":"back","start":1.08},{"w":"to","start":1.413},{"w":"NLP,","start":1.747},{"w":"Simply","start":2.08},{"w":"Explained.","start":2.68},{"w":"This","start":3.48},{"w":"is","start":3.76},{"w":"unit","start":3.96},{"w":"1,","start":4.333},{"w":"lesson","start":4.707},{"w":"2:","start":5.08},{"w":"tokenization.","start":5.44}]},{"id":"c02","start":6.915,"end":15.836,"marks":{},"text":"Last time we climbed the staircase of NLP. Today we stand on the very first step, and look closely at how text gets cut into pieces.","words":[{"w":"Last","start":6.915},{"w":"time","start":7.235},{"w":"we","start":7.515},{"w":"climbed","start":7.775},{"w":"the","start":8.035},{"w":"staircase","start":8.195},{"w":"of","start":8.835},{"w":"NLP.","start":9.475},{"w":"Today","start":10.115},{"w":"we","start":10.755},{"w":"stand","start":10.995},{"w":"on","start":11.355},{"w":"the","start":11.475},{"w":"very","start":11.675},{"w":"first","start":11.955},{"w":"step,","start":12.275},{"w":"and","start":12.675},{"w":"look","start":12.915},{"w":"closely","start":13.155},{"w":"at","start":13.635},{"w":"how","start":13.795},{"w":"text","start":13.995},{"w":"gets","start":14.475},{"w":"cut","start":14.755},{"w":"into","start":15.035},{"w":"pieces.","start":15.235}]}],"title":"Welcome","shortTitle":"Welcome","props":{"kicker":"Unit 1 · Lesson 2","title":"Tokenization","subtitle":"How text becomes pieces a model can use"},"start":0.6,"end":15.836,"startFrame":0,"durationInFrames":503},{"id":"idea","kind":"core","component":"BigIdea","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c03","start":16.767,"end":22.826,"marks":{},"text":"Here is the idea to hold on to. A model never reads text the way you do. It reads tokens.","words":[{"w":"Here","start":16.767},{"w":"is","start":17.047},{"w":"the","start":17.167},{"w":"idea","start":17.367},{"w":"to","start":17.807},{"w":"hold","start":17.967},{"w":"on","start":18.287},{"w":"to.","start":18.487},{"w":"A","start":18.847},{"w":"model","start":19.087},{"w":"never","start":19.567},{"w":"reads","start":19.847},{"w":"text","start":20.227},{"w":"the","start":20.607},{"w":"way","start":20.767},{"w":"you","start":20.927},{"w":"do.","start":21.127},{"w":"It","start":21.407},{"w":"reads","start":21.647},{"w":"tokens.","start":22.127}]}],"title":"The big idea","shortTitle":"The big idea","props":{"kicker":"Key idea","text":"A model never reads text. It reads tokens.","highlight":["tokens."]},"start":16.767,"end":22.826,"startFrame":503,"durationInFrames":209},{"id":"token","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c04","start":23.733,"end":32.58,"marks":{},"text":"So what is a token? A token is one unit of text that a model works with. It can be a whole word, a piece of a word, or a punctuation mark.","words":[{"w":"So","start":23.733},{"w":"what","start":23.973},{"w":"is","start":24.173},{"w":"a","start":24.373},{"w":"token?","start":24.493},{"w":"A","start":25.173},{"w":"token","start":25.413},{"w":"is","start":25.973},{"w":"one","start":26.173},{"w":"unit","start":26.453},{"w":"of","start":26.773},{"w":"text","start":26.933},{"w":"that","start":27.333},{"w":"a","start":27.453},{"w":"model","start":27.573},{"w":"works","start":27.973},{"w":"with.","start":28.333},{"w":"It","start":28.653},{"w":"can","start":28.893},{"w":"be","start":29.053},{"w":"a","start":29.213},{"w":"whole","start":29.373},{"w":"word,","start":29.733},{"w":"a","start":30.013},{"w":"piece","start":30.213},{"w":"of","start":30.493},{"w":"a","start":30.613},{"w":"word,","start":30.773},{"w":"or","start":31.093},{"w":"a","start":31.293},{"w":"punctuation","start":31.413},{"w":"mark.","start":32.213}]},{"id":"c05","start":32.98,"end":42.955,"marks":{},"text":"Take the sentence \"I don't like rain!\" A typical tokenizer cuts it into six tokens: I, do, n't, like, rain, and the exclamation mark.","words":[{"w":"Take","start":32.98},{"w":"the","start":33.22},{"w":"sentence","start":33.42},{"w":"\"I","start":33.94},{"w":"don't","start":34.1},{"w":"like","start":34.38},{"w":"rain!\"","start":34.66},{"w":"A","start":35.22},{"w":"typical","start":35.46},{"w":"tokenizer","start":36.02},{"w":"cuts","start":36.74},{"w":"it","start":37.02},{"w":"into","start":37.18},{"w":"six","start":37.38},{"w":"tokens:","start":37.66},{"w":"I,","start":38.58},{"w":"do,","start":38.94},{"w":"n't,","start":39.8},{"w":"like,","start":40.66},{"w":"rain,","start":41.02},{"w":"and","start":41.5},{"w":"the","start":41.66},{"w":"exclamation","start":41.82},{"w":"mark.","start":42.58}]},{"id":"c06","start":43.355,"end":52.187,"marks":{},"text":"Think of it like chopping vegetables before you cook. You can't cook a whole pumpkin in one go, and the size you cut the pieces into changes everything.","words":[{"w":"Think","start":43.355},{"w":"of","start":43.555},{"w":"it","start":43.675},{"w":"like","start":43.875},{"w":"chopping","start":44.368},{"w":"vegetables","start":44.862},{"w":"before","start":45.355},{"w":"you","start":45.635},{"w":"cook.","start":45.875},{"w":"You","start":46.355},{"w":"can't","start":46.635},{"w":"cook","start":46.955},{"w":"a","start":47.195},{"w":"whole","start":47.355},{"w":"pumpkin","start":47.595},{"w":"in","start":48.155},{"w":"one","start":48.355},{"w":"go,","start":48.595},{"w":"and","start":48.955},{"w":"the","start":49.195},{"w":"size","start":49.355},{"w":"you","start":49.715},{"w":"cut","start":49.915},{"w":"the","start":50.155},{"w":"pieces","start":50.315},{"w":"into","start":50.715},{"w":"changes","start":50.955},{"w":"everything.","start":51.595}]}],"title":"What is a token?","shortTitle":"What is a token?","props":{"kicker":"Definition","term":"Token","definition":"One unit of text a model works with: a word, a piece of a word, or a punctuation mark.","example":"I · do · n't · like · rain · !","analogy":"Chopping vegetables before cooking: the size of the pieces matters."},"start":23.733,"end":52.187,"startFrame":712,"durationInFrames":881},{"id":"spaces","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c07","start":53.1,"end":59.107,"marks":{},"text":"The obvious first idea is to split the text wherever there is a space. Let's see where that goes wrong.","words":[{"w":"The","start":53.1},{"w":"obvious","start":53.26},{"w":"first","start":53.78},{"w":"idea","start":54.06},{"w":"is","start":54.62},{"w":"to","start":54.78},{"w":"split","start":54.94},{"w":"the","start":55.3},{"w":"text","start":55.46},{"w":"wherever","start":55.9},{"w":"there","start":56.3},{"w":"is","start":56.5},{"w":"a","start":56.66},{"w":"space.","start":56.78},{"w":"Let's","start":57.42},{"w":"see","start":57.82},{"w":"where","start":58.02},{"w":"that","start":58.18},{"w":"goes","start":58.38},{"w":"wrong.","start":58.74}]},{"id":"c08","start":59.507,"end":65.33,"marks":{},"text":"\"traffic\" with an exclamation mark stays glued together, so the punctuation becomes part of the word.","words":[{"w":"\"traffic\"","start":59.507},{"w":"with","start":60.067},{"w":"an","start":60.267},{"w":"exclamation","start":60.387},{"w":"mark","start":61.107},{"w":"stays","start":61.467},{"w":"glued","start":61.847},{"w":"together,","start":62.227},{"w":"so","start":62.787},{"w":"the","start":62.947},{"w":"punctuation","start":63.107},{"w":"becomes","start":63.987},{"w":"part","start":64.507},{"w":"of","start":64.707},{"w":"the","start":64.827},{"w":"word.","start":64.987}]},{"id":"c09","start":65.73,"end":70.069,"marks":{},"text":"\"don't\" stays as one piece, even though it really means two words: do and not.","words":[{"w":"\"don't\"","start":65.73},{"w":"stays","start":66.09},{"w":"as","start":66.49},{"w":"one","start":66.69},{"w":"piece,","start":66.89},{"w":"even","start":67.33},{"w":"though","start":67.61},{"w":"it","start":67.81},{"w":"really","start":67.93},{"w":"means","start":68.29},{"w":"two","start":68.61},{"w":"words:","start":68.85},{"w":"do","start":69.33},{"w":"and","start":69.53},{"w":"not.","start":69.69}]},{"id":"c10","start":70.469,"end":76.155,"marks":{},"text":"In \"Doctor Rao\", the dot after \"Dr\" does not end a sentence, but a simple splitter can't tell.","words":[{"w":"In","start":70.469},{"w":"\"Doctor","start":70.629},{"w":"Rao\",","start":71.049},{"w":"the","start":71.469},{"w":"dot","start":71.749},{"w":"after","start":72.069},{"w":"\"Dr\"","start":72.469},{"w":"does","start":72.869},{"w":"not","start":73.149},{"w":"end","start":73.309},{"w":"a","start":73.509},{"w":"sentence,","start":73.629},{"w":"but","start":74.189},{"w":"a","start":74.429},{"w":"simple","start":74.549},{"w":"splitter","start":74.949},{"w":"can't","start":75.509},{"w":"tell.","start":75.869}]},{"id":"c11","start":76.555,"end":81.84,"marks":{},"text":"And \"New York\" is one name, but splitting on spaces breaks it into two unrelated words.","words":[{"w":"And","start":76.555},{"w":"\"New","start":76.822},{"w":"York\"","start":77.088},{"w":"is","start":77.355},{"w":"one","start":77.555},{"w":"name,","start":77.835},{"w":"but","start":78.155},{"w":"splitting","start":78.435},{"w":"on","start":78.915},{"w":"spaces","start":79.115},{"w":"breaks","start":79.595},{"w":"it","start":79.995},{"w":"into","start":80.155},{"w":"two","start":80.395},{"w":"unrelated","start":80.635},{"w":"words.","start":81.355}]}],"title":"Why spaces aren't enough","shortTitle":"Why spaces aren't enough","props":{"kicker":"First attempt","title":"Just split on spaces?","columns":["Text","Problem"],"rows":[["traffic!","punctuation glued on"],["don't","two words in one"],["Dr. Rao","a dot that doesn't end a sentence"],["New York","one name, split in two"]],"highlight":[]},"start":53.1,"end":81.84,"startFrame":1593,"durationInFrames":890},{"id":"sizes","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c12","start":82.767,"end":90.788,"marks":{},"text":"Fixing those cases with rules helps, but there is a bigger question: how big should a piece be? Let's cut the word \"raindrops\" three ways.","words":[{"w":"Fixing","start":82.767},{"w":"those","start":83.167},{"w":"cases","start":83.407},{"w":"with","start":83.847},{"w":"rules","start":84.047},{"w":"helps,","start":84.447},{"w":"but","start":84.887},{"w":"there","start":85.047},{"w":"is","start":85.247},{"w":"a","start":85.367},{"w":"bigger","start":85.727},{"w":"question:","start":86.087},{"w":"how","start":86.447},{"w":"big","start":86.727},{"w":"should","start":87.087},{"w":"a","start":87.247},{"w":"piece","start":87.407},{"w":"be?","start":87.727},{"w":"Let's","start":88.047},{"w":"cut","start":88.487},{"w":"the","start":88.767},{"w":"word","start":88.927},{"w":"\"raindrops\"","start":89.207},{"w":"three","start":90.047},{"w":"ways.","start":90.367}]},{"id":"c13","start":91.188,"end":100.915,"marks":{},"text":"Option one: single characters. The vocabulary is tiny, and nothing is ever unknown. But every sentence turns into a very long sequence of letters.","words":[{"w":"Option","start":91.188},{"w":"one:","start":91.748},{"w":"single","start":92.028},{"w":"characters.","start":92.588},{"w":"The","start":93.241},{"w":"vocabulary","start":93.895},{"w":"is","start":94.548},{"w":"tiny,","start":94.748},{"w":"and","start":95.268},{"w":"nothing","start":95.508},{"w":"is","start":95.908},{"w":"ever","start":96.108},{"w":"unknown.","start":96.428},{"w":"But","start":97.188},{"w":"every","start":97.428},{"w":"sentence","start":97.788},{"w":"turns","start":98.388},{"w":"into","start":98.788},{"w":"a","start":98.988},{"w":"very","start":99.148},{"w":"long","start":99.428},{"w":"sequence","start":99.748},{"w":"of","start":100.228},{"w":"letters.","start":100.388}]},{"id":"c14","start":101.315,"end":110.91,"marks":{},"text":"Option two: whole words. Each piece has meaning, but there are millions of words, names and typos. Any word missing from the list becomes \"unknown\".","words":[{"w":"Option","start":101.315},{"w":"two:","start":101.795},{"w":"whole","start":102.235},{"w":"words.","start":102.635},{"w":"Each","start":103.235},{"w":"piece","start":103.635},{"w":"has","start":103.995},{"w":"meaning,","start":104.235},{"w":"but","start":104.675},{"w":"there","start":104.875},{"w":"are","start":105.075},{"w":"millions","start":105.315},{"w":"of","start":105.795},{"w":"words,","start":105.955},{"w":"names","start":106.515},{"w":"and","start":106.915},{"w":"typos.","start":107.155},{"w":"Any","start":107.955},{"w":"word","start":108.355},{"w":"missing","start":108.635},{"w":"from","start":109.035},{"w":"the","start":109.195},{"w":"list","start":109.315},{"w":"becomes","start":109.675},{"w":"\"unknown\".","start":110.195}]},{"id":"c15","start":111.31,"end":123.462,"marks":{"verdict":120.59},"text":"Option three: subwords. \"raindrops\" becomes \"rain\" plus \"drops\". Common words stay whole, and rare words are built from smaller pieces. That balance is why modern models use subwords.","words":[{"w":"Option","start":111.31},{"w":"three:","start":111.87},{"w":"subwords.","start":112.35},{"w":"\"raindrops\"","start":113.27},{"w":"becomes","start":114.19},{"w":"\"rain\"","start":114.71},{"w":"plus","start":115.11},{"w":"\"drops\".","start":115.55},{"w":"Common","start":116.35},{"w":"words","start":116.87},{"w":"stay","start":117.23},{"w":"whole,","start":117.55},{"w":"and","start":117.87},{"w":"rare","start":118.11},{"w":"words","start":118.47},{"w":"are","start":118.75},{"w":"built","start":118.91},{"w":"from","start":119.23},{"w":"smaller","start":119.43},{"w":"pieces.","start":119.87},{"w":"That","start":120.59},{"w":"balance","start":120.83},{"w":"is","start":121.35},{"w":"why","start":121.51},{"w":"modern","start":121.71},{"w":"models","start":122.15},{"w":"use","start":122.55},{"w":"subwords.","start":122.79}]}],"title":"Characters, words or subwords?","shortTitle":"How AI decides the size of a word piece","props":{"kicker":"How big is a piece?","title":"Three ways to cut “raindrops”","columns":[{"title":"Characters","items":["r · a · i · n · d · r · o · p · s","tiny vocabulary","very long sequences"],"tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Words","items":["raindrops","unseen words become unknown"],"tone":"bad"},{"title":"Subwords","items":["rain · drops","common words stay whole","rare words split into pieces"],"tone":"good"}],"verdict":{"text":"Modern models use subwords","at":"c15@verdict"}},"start":82.767,"end":123.462,"startFrame":2483,"durationInFrames":1248},{"id":"bpe","kind":"core","component":"Steps","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c16","start":124.367,"end":132.007,"marks":{},"text":"The most popular way to build a subword vocabulary is called Byte Pair Encoding, or BPE. It has just four steps.","words":[{"w":"The","start":124.367},{"w":"most","start":124.527},{"w":"popular","start":124.767},{"w":"way","start":125.247},{"w":"to","start":125.407},{"w":"build","start":125.567},{"w":"a","start":125.807},{"w":"subword","start":126.287},{"w":"vocabulary","start":126.767},{"w":"is","start":127.247},{"w":"called","start":127.447},{"w":"Byte","start":127.847},{"w":"Pair","start":128.247},{"w":"Encoding,","start":128.647},{"w":"or","start":129.047},{"w":"BPE.","start":129.507},{"w":"It","start":129.967},{"w":"has","start":130.527},{"w":"just","start":130.767},{"w":"four","start":131.087},{"w":"steps.","start":131.407}]},{"id":"c17","start":132.407,"end":135.732,"marks":{},"text":"Split: start by breaking every word into single characters.","words":[{"w":"Split:","start":132.407},{"w":"start","start":132.927},{"w":"by","start":133.287},{"w":"breaking","start":133.447},{"w":"every","start":133.887},{"w":"word","start":134.167},{"w":"into","start":134.447},{"w":"single","start":134.647},{"w":"characters.","start":135.087}]},{"id":"c18","start":136.132,"end":139.665,"marks":{},"text":"Count: count how often each pair of neighbouring pieces appears.","words":[{"w":"Count:","start":136.132},{"w":"count","start":136.532},{"w":"how","start":136.932},{"w":"often","start":137.172},{"w":"each","start":137.572},{"w":"pair","start":137.812},{"w":"of","start":138.052},{"w":"neighbouring","start":138.132},{"w":"pieces","start":138.612},{"w":"appears.","start":139.092}]},{"id":"c19","start":140.065,"end":143.344,"marks":{},"text":"Merge: glue the most common pair together into a new piece.","words":[{"w":"Merge:","start":140.065},{"w":"glue","start":140.625},{"w":"the","start":140.985},{"w":"most","start":141.105},{"w":"common","start":141.345},{"w":"pair","start":141.705},{"w":"together","start":141.985},{"w":"into","start":142.385},{"w":"a","start":142.585},{"w":"new","start":142.705},{"w":"piece.","start":142.905}]},{"id":"c20","start":143.744,"end":148.618,"marks":{},"text":"Repeat: count again and merge again, until the vocabulary is as big as you want.","words":[{"w":"Repeat:","start":143.744},{"w":"count","start":144.424},{"w":"again","start":144.784},{"w":"and","start":145.024},{"w":"merge","start":145.264},{"w":"again,","start":145.664},{"w":"until","start":146.024},{"w":"the","start":146.451},{"w":"vocabulary","start":146.877},{"w":"is","start":147.304},{"w":"as","start":147.464},{"w":"big","start":147.624},{"w":"as","start":147.904},{"w":"you","start":148.064},{"w":"want.","start":148.264}]}],"title":"Byte Pair Encoding","shortTitle":"Byte Pair Encoding","props":{"kicker":"Byte Pair Encoding","title":"How a subword vocabulary is built","steps":[{"label":"Split","detail":"every word into characters"},{"label":"Count","detail":"pairs of neighbours"},{"label":"Merge","detail":"the most common pair"},{"label":"Repeat","detail":"until the vocabulary is big enough"}]},"start":124.367,"end":148.618,"startFrame":3731,"durationInFrames":755},{"id":"worked","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c21","start":149.533,"end":158.774,"marks":{},"text":"Let's try it on a tiny example. Our text contains \"rain\" nine times, \"rainy\" four times, \"raining\" five times and \"train\" three times.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":149.533},{"w":"try","start":149.813},{"w":"it","start":150.053},{"w":"on","start":150.253},{"w":"a","start":150.333},{"w":"tiny","start":150.453},{"w":"example.","start":150.813},{"w":"Our","start":151.573},{"w":"text","start":151.773},{"w":"contains","start":152.253},{"w":"\"rain\"","start":152.813},{"w":"nine","start":153.213},{"w":"times,","start":153.653},{"w":"\"rainy\"","start":154.253},{"w":"four","start":154.813},{"w":"times,","start":155.133},{"w":"\"raining\"","start":155.773},{"w":"five","start":156.373},{"w":"times","start":156.813},{"w":"and","start":157.213},{"w":"\"train\"","start":157.453},{"w":"three","start":157.933},{"w":"times.","start":158.293}]},{"id":"c22","start":159.174,"end":167.831,"marks":{},"text":"The most common pair is \"i\" followed by \"n\": twenty-six times, because \"raining\" contains it twice. So \"i\" and \"n\" merge into \"in\".","words":[{"w":"The","start":159.174},{"w":"most","start":159.294},{"w":"common","start":159.534},{"w":"pair","start":159.894},{"w":"is","start":160.214},{"w":"\"i\"","start":160.414},{"w":"followed","start":160.774},{"w":"by","start":161.264},{"w":"\"n\":","start":161.754},{"w":"twenty-six","start":162.244},{"w":"times,","start":162.734},{"w":"because","start":163.134},{"w":"\"raining\"","start":163.454},{"w":"contains","start":163.974},{"w":"it","start":164.494},{"w":"twice.","start":164.694},{"w":"So","start":165.334},{"w":"\"i\"","start":165.734},{"w":"and","start":166.067},{"w":"\"n\"","start":166.401},{"w":"merge","start":166.734},{"w":"into","start":167.1},{"w":"\"in\".","start":167.465}]},{"id":"c23","start":168.231,"end":172.52,"marks":{},"text":"Next, \"r\" followed by \"a\" appears twenty-one times, so it becomes \"ra\".","words":[{"w":"Next,","start":168.231},{"w":"\"r\"","start":168.671},{"w":"followed","start":169.111},{"w":"by","start":169.551},{"w":"\"a\"","start":169.691},{"w":"appears","start":169.831},{"w":"twenty-one","start":170.351},{"w":"times,","start":170.871},{"w":"so","start":171.271},{"w":"it","start":171.471},{"w":"becomes","start":171.631},{"w":"\"ra\".","start":172.076}]},{"id":"c24","start":172.92,"end":179.422,"marks":{},"text":"Then \"ra\" and \"in\" merge into \"rain\". After just three merges, the whole word \"rain\" is a single token.","words":[{"w":"Then","start":172.92},{"w":"\"ra\"","start":173.28},{"w":"and","start":173.64},{"w":"\"in\"","start":173.84},{"w":"merge","start":174.16},{"w":"into","start":174.56},{"w":"\"rain\".","start":174.84},{"w":"After","start":175.48},{"w":"just","start":175.96},{"w":"three","start":176.2},{"w":"merges,","start":176.44},{"w":"the","start":177},{"w":"whole","start":177.2},{"w":"word","start":177.52},{"w":"\"rain\"","start":177.8},{"w":"is","start":178.2},{"w":"a","start":178.36},{"w":"single","start":178.52},{"w":"token.","start":178.92}]}],"title":"BPE, worked example","shortTitle":"BPE, worked example","props":{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"rain ×9 · rainy ×4 · raining ×5 · train ×3","columns":["Merge","Seen","“raining” becomes"],"rows":[["i + n → in","26 times","r a in in g"],["r + a → ra","21 times","ra in in g"],["ra + in → rain","21 times","rain in g"]],"highlight":[{"row":2,"col":2}]},"start":149.533,"end":179.422,"startFrame":4486,"durationInFrames":924},{"id":"count","kind":"core","component":"BarChart","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c25","start":180.333,"end":183.898,"marks":{},"text":"Now compare how many pieces each approach needs for \"raindrops\".","words":[{"w":"Now","start":180.333},{"w":"compare","start":180.613},{"w":"how","start":181.013},{"w":"many","start":181.213},{"w":"pieces","start":181.453},{"w":"each","start":181.893},{"w":"approach","start":182.093},{"w":"needs","start":182.573},{"w":"for","start":182.893},{"w":"\"raindrops\".","start":183.093}]},{"id":"c26","start":184.298,"end":188.894,"marks":{},"text":"As characters, it is nine tokens: long, and each letter means very little.","words":[{"w":"As","start":184.298},{"w":"characters,","start":184.498},{"w":"it","start":185.138},{"w":"is","start":185.298},{"w":"nine","start":185.458},{"w":"tokens:","start":185.818},{"w":"long,","start":186.738},{"w":"and","start":187.098},{"w":"each","start":187.338},{"w":"letter","start":187.618},{"w":"means","start":187.938},{"w":"very","start":188.298},{"w":"little.","start":188.578}]},{"id":"c27","start":189.294,"end":192.325,"marks":{},"text":"As subwords, it is just two: \"rain\" and \"drops\".","words":[{"w":"As","start":189.294},{"w":"subwords,","start":189.654},{"w":"it","start":190.014},{"w":"is","start":190.174},{"w":"just","start":190.334},{"w":"two:","start":190.574},{"w":"\"rain\"","start":191.054},{"w":"and","start":191.494},{"w":"\"drops\".","start":191.694}]},{"id":"c28","start":192.725,"end":201.805,"marks":{},"text":"As a whole word, it is one, but only if \"raindrops\" happens to be in the vocabulary. Subwords give short sequences, with no unknown words.","words":[{"w":"As","start":192.725},{"w":"a","start":192.885},{"w":"whole","start":193.005},{"w":"word,","start":193.325},{"w":"it","start":193.605},{"w":"is","start":193.845},{"w":"one,","start":194.045},{"w":"but","start":194.405},{"w":"only","start":194.685},{"w":"if","start":195.005},{"w":"\"raindrops\"","start":195.285},{"w":"happens","start":196.085},{"w":"to","start":196.485},{"w":"be","start":196.605},{"w":"in","start":196.765},{"w":"the","start":197.315},{"w":"vocabulary.","start":197.865},{"w":"Subwords","start":198.415},{"w":"give","start":198.965},{"w":"short","start":199.205},{"w":"sequences,","start":199.525},{"w":"with","start":200.285},{"w":"no","start":200.485},{"w":"unknown","start":200.765},{"w":"words.","start":201.365}]}],"title":"How many pieces?","shortTitle":"How many pieces?","props":{"kicker":"The trade-off","title":"How many pieces is “raindrops”?","unit":"tokens","bars":[{"label":"Characters","value":9},{"label":"Subwords","value":2},{"label":"Words","value":1}],"note":"Subwords: short sequences, and no unknown words."},"start":180.333,"end":201.805,"startFrame":5410,"durationInFrames":672},{"id":"quiz","kind":"quiz","component":"Quiz","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c29","start":202.733,"end":209.511,"marks":{},"text":"Time for a quick quiz. A subword tokenizer meets the word \"unfriendliness\" for the first time. What happens?","words":[{"w":"Time","start":202.733},{"w":"for","start":203.053},{"w":"a","start":203.353},{"w":"quick","start":203.653},{"w":"quiz.","start":203.953},{"w":"A","start":204.253},{"w":"subword","start":204.493},{"w":"tokenizer","start":205.053},{"w":"meets","start":205.773},{"w":"the","start":206.093},{"w":"word","start":206.253},{"w":"\"unfriendliness\"","start":206.533},{"w":"for","start":207.453},{"w":"the","start":207.573},{"w":"first","start":207.733},{"w":"time.","start":208.093},{"w":"What","start":208.573},{"w":"happens?","start":208.853}]},{"id":"c30","start":209.911,"end":215.836,"marks":{},"text":"Pause the video and choose. Does it mark the word as unknown, split it into known pieces, or skip it?","words":[{"w":"Pause","start":209.911},{"w":"the","start":210.231},{"w":"video","start":210.511},{"w":"and","start":210.791},{"w":"choose.","start":210.991},{"w":"Does","start":211.511},{"w":"it","start":211.831},{"w":"mark","start":212.031},{"w":"the","start":212.271},{"w":"word","start":212.471},{"w":"as","start":212.711},{"w":"unknown,","start":212.951},{"w":"split","start":213.591},{"w":"it","start":213.991},{"w":"into","start":214.151},{"w":"known","start":214.351},{"w":"pieces,","start":214.631},{"w":"or","start":215.111},{"w":"skip","start":215.311},{"w":"it?","start":215.671}]},{"id":"c31","start":219.236,"end":225.216,"marks":{},"text":"It splits it into known pieces: un, friend, li, ness. Pieces it has seen many times before.","words":[{"w":"It","start":219.236},{"w":"splits","start":219.356},{"w":"it","start":219.716},{"w":"into","start":219.876},{"w":"known","start":220.076},{"w":"pieces:","start":220.356},{"w":"un,","start":220.892},{"w":"friend,","start":221.428},{"w":"li,","start":221.964},{"w":"ness.","start":222.5},{"w":"Pieces","start":223.036},{"w":"it","start":223.556},{"w":"has","start":223.716},{"w":"seen","start":223.836},{"w":"many","start":224.076},{"w":"times","start":224.396},{"w":"before.","start":224.796}]}],"title":"Quick quiz","shortTitle":"Quick quiz: what does AI do with a brand-new word?","props":{"kicker":"Pause and predict","question":"A subword tokenizer meets “unfriendliness” for the first time. What happens?","options":["It marks it as unknown","It splits it into known pieces","It skips the word"],"answer":1,"explain":"un · friend · li · ness: pieces it has seen many times before."},"start":202.733,"end":225.216,"startFrame":6082,"durationInFrames":702},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","component":"Recap","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c32","start":226.133,"end":230.067,"marks":{},"text":"Let's recap. A token is one unit of text that a model reads.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":226.133},{"w":"recap.","start":226.533},{"w":"A","start":227.133},{"w":"token","start":227.373},{"w":"is","start":227.853},{"w":"one","start":228.053},{"w":"unit","start":228.293},{"w":"of","start":228.613},{"w":"text","start":228.733},{"w":"that","start":229.053},{"w":"a","start":229.133},{"w":"model","start":229.253},{"w":"reads.","start":229.613}]},{"id":"c33","start":230.467,"end":236.325,"marks":{},"text":"Splitting on spaces alone is not enough: punctuation, contractions and names get in the way.","words":[{"w":"Splitting","start":230.467},{"w":"on","start":230.907},{"w":"spaces","start":231.067},{"w":"alone","start":231.547},{"w":"is","start":232.027},{"w":"not","start":232.227},{"w":"enough:","start":232.467},{"w":"punctuation,","start":232.987},{"w":"contractions","start":234.187},{"w":"and","start":235.027},{"w":"names","start":235.227},{"w":"get","start":235.587},{"w":"in","start":235.787},{"w":"the","start":235.907},{"w":"way.","start":236.067}]},{"id":"c34","start":236.725,"end":242.479,"marks":{},"text":"Subwords balance the two extremes: shorter than characters, and never unknown like whole words.","words":[{"w":"Subwords","start":236.725},{"w":"balance","start":237.365},{"w":"the","start":237.805},{"w":"two","start":237.965},{"w":"extremes:","start":238.205},{"w":"shorter","start":239.045},{"w":"than","start":239.485},{"w":"characters,","start":239.685},{"w":"and","start":240.405},{"w":"never","start":240.605},{"w":"unknown","start":240.925},{"w":"like","start":241.485},{"w":"whole","start":241.725},{"w":"words.","start":242.005}]},{"id":"c35","star